  "id": "psychological-atomism",
  "term": "psychological atomism",
  "definition": "Psychological atomism is a historical composition view of mind that treats mental life as built from tiny mental particles or “mind-dust” spread throughout nature alongside material atoms. On this view, these mental elements can under suitable conditions make up the conscious mind.",
